rror / warning counts.\n- Step 6 result: one row per forbidden token (token, hit count, matching lines if any).\n- Step 7 result: list of forbidden modules and which (if any) appeared in sys.modules.\n- Step 8 result: evaluator rule order observed, with file path and line range for each rule.\n- Final marker line: PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_LOCAL_VALIDATION_PASSED or PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_LOCAL_VALIDATION_FAILED.\n\n9b. claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/48_2E1C_ALPHA_VALIDATION_GO_NO_GO.md\nExactly one line: PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_LOCAL_VALIDATION_PASSED or PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_LOCAL_VALIDATION_FAILED. No other content.\n\nStep 10 - safety guarantees. Do not modify any file under v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness/ or v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness/. Do not modify any file outside the allowed_output_prefixes. Do not commit. Do not push. Do not run any subprocess other than pytest, python -c, and grep / rg. Do not start the legacy trainer venv. Do not import any legacy module. Do not access Redis. Do not access network. Do not read .env. Do not enable live trading.\n\nIf any step fails, write PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_LOCAL_VALIDATION_FAILED, leave 46_2E1C_ALPHA_GO_NO_GO.md untouched, and stop. Do not invoke remediation directly; remediation is a separate task under REQ_0007 autofix scope.",
